Node 14 doesn't have `structuredClone` (added in Node 17). Options:

**1. Use the v8 serializer (built-in, handles Dates, Maps, Sets, etc.):**

```js
const v8 = require('v8');

if (typeof structuredClone !== 'function') {
  global.structuredClone = (obj) => v8.deserialize(v8.serialize(obj));
}
```

**2. Install a polyfill package:**

```bash
npm install @ungap/structured-clone
```

```js
const structuredClone = require('@ungap/structured-clone');
```

**3. JSON round-trip (only if your data is plain JSON — loses Dates, Maps, undefined, functions):**

```js
global.structuredClone = (obj) => JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj));
```

Option 1 is the closest match to native behavior since it uses the same serialization mechanism Node's real `structuredClone` is built on. Note it won't clone functions or DOM nodes (which don't exist in Node anyway), same as the native version.

